{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38348538",
      "title": "Managing State",
      "sourceHash": "ee9fb0ea1cd9c85c3a458cfaa2ca2bb72f9fdaa21a128615bfc3180dec3593fc",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "So now that we're handling events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 7.29,
          "en": "it's time to start managing state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.29,
          "end": 10.203,
          "en": "because that's the next task we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.25,
          "end": 13.2,
          "en": "Now for that, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.2,
          "end": 17.01,
          "en": "we first of all have to identify the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.01,
          "end": 18.54,
          "en": "that should be managed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.54,
          "end": 20.58,
          "en": "And of course, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.58,
          "end": 23.1,
          "en": "there typically isn't just a single right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.1,
          "end": 26.1,
          "en": "or wrong way of building such an application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.1,
          "end": 29.55,
          "en": "But I would argue that we probably have some state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.55,
          "end": 31.893,
          "en": "to manage in the userInput component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.79,
          "end": 35.64,
          "en": "All these values entered by the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.64,
          "end": 38.19,
          "en": "should be managed as state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.19,
          "end": 42.24,
          "en": "We need them as state so that we can submit them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.24,
          "end": 44.133,
          "en": "when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.87,
          "end": 48,
          "en": "And we also need them as state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48,
          "end": 51.543,
          "en": "so that we can reset them if the reset button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.18,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "Therefore, in this userInput JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 59.493,
          "en": "in this userInput component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.42,
          "end": 62.94,
          "en": "I'll use useState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.94,
          "end": 66.96,
          "en": "this useState hook which is imported from react,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.96,
          "end": 68.733,
          "en": "to start managing some state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.9,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "And now the question just is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 76.28999999999999,
          "en": "which state values do we want to manage?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.28999999999999,
          "end": 81.28999999999999,
          "en": "And the answer is, well, one for every input, most likely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.16,
          "end": 87.51,
          "en": "because we need to store and use all these input values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.51,
          "end": 89.07,
          "en": "And it now in the end comes down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.07,
          "end": 90.9,
          "en": "to your personal preference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.9,
          "end": 94.05,
          "en": "whether you want to manage one state object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.05,
          "end": 97.08,
          "en": "with multiple keys inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.08,
          "end": 99.723,
          "en": "one key per input element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.07,
          "end": 103.68,
          "en": "or if you wanna have multiple state slices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.68,
          "end": 106.22999999999999,
          "en": "by calling useState multiple times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.22999999999999,
          "end": 108.243,
          "en": "once for every input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.25999999999999,
          "end": 110.67,
          "en": "It's totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.67,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "And here, I'll go for the one bigger state object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 116.1,
          "en": "which is being managed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.1,
          "end": 119.703,
          "en": "where I'll have one key per input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.35,
          "end": 125.28,
          "en": "So for example, we could add a key named current-savings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.28,
          "end": 127.83,
          "en": "here to this object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.83,
          "end": 130.11,
          "en": "Not like this though, since the dash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.11,
          "end": 134.073,
          "en": "is not an allowed character like this in a property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.97,
          "end": 137.64,
          "en": "Instead, you have to wrap it in quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.64,
          "end": 140.13,
          "en": "This is valid JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.13,
          "end": 142.5,
          "en": "and allows you to use property names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.5,
          "end": 145.17000000000002,
          "en": "which otherwise couldn't be used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.17000000000002,
          "end": 148.05,
          "en": "for example names that include such a dash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.05,
          "end": 150.6,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.6,
          "end": 153.933,
          "en": "use camel case notation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.82999999999998,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "That is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 160.29,
          "en": "But I'll go for the identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.29,
          "end": 162.09300000000002,
          "en": "I'm also using on my input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.38,
          "end": 166.353,
          "en": "And then we need a value for that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.19,
          "end": 169.35,
          "en": "And for the current savings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.35,
          "end": 173.73,
          "en": "so in the end, our starting amount of savings we have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.73,
          "end": 177.78,
          "en": "we could start with a value of 1,000 or 10,000",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.78,
          "end": 179.19,
          "en": "or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.19,
          "end": 181.267,
          "en": "Here, I'll go for 10,000.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.64,
          "end": 184.56,
          "en": "Now that's of course not the only key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.56,
          "end": 189.513,
          "en": "Instead, we also have this yearly-contribution input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.38,
          "end": 193.2,
          "en": "which in the end is about getting that amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.2,
          "end": 195.3,
          "en": "that will be added every year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.3,
          "end": 197.74,
          "en": "We could set this to 1,200",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.66,
          "end": 201.183,
          "en": "so that we save 100 bucks per month.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.41,
          "end": 206.13,
          "en": "The next key value pair in this state object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.13,
          "end": 209.34,
          "en": "will be the key value pair for the third input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.34,
          "end": 211.923,
          "en": "which is the expected return rate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.21,
          "end": 215.61,
          "en": "So therefore, I'll use this identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.61,
          "end": 219.663,
          "en": "And here, we could set this to seven percent, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.22,
          "end": 224.22,
          "en": "And then the last key I wanna manage here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.22,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "is for the last input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 229.143,
          "en": "which is the duration over which we wanna save.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.19,
          "end": 232.23,
          "en": "Hence, I'll use duration as a key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 232.23,
          "end": 234.993,
          "en": "and maybe set this to 10 years as a default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.57999999999998,
          "end": 239.43,
          "en": "With that, we're creating this state object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.43,
          "end": 242.76,
          "en": "And as you learned, useState now returns an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 242.76,
          "end": 244.953,
          "en": "with exactly two elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.02,
          "end": 249.03,
          "en": "And we can use array destructuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.03,
          "end": 251.55,
          "en": "to get elements out of this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 251.55,
          "end": 254.103,
          "en": "And here, we'll get the userInput",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.56,
          "end": 260.16,
          "en": "and then a setUserInput state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.16,
          "end": 261.18,
          "en": "though, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.18,
          "end": 264.063,
          "en": "these names of these elements are up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 265.26,
          "end": 268.98,
          "en": "Now the idea now is to call set userInput",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.98,
          "end": 271.81,
          "en": "whenever the inputChangeHandler is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 273.42,
          "end": 276.6,
          "en": "because, there, we want to update this state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 276.6,
          "end": 278.19,
          "en": "this state object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.19,
          "end": 282.303,
          "en": "and store the latest entered values in that state object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.89,
          "end": 285.543,
          "en": "Therefore, in inputChangeHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 286.44,
          "end": 289.71,
          "en": "we want to set our state to a new object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 289.71,
          "end": 293.04,
          "en": "which of course should be based on the old object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.04,
          "end": 296.22,
          "en": "because we don't want to discard the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.22,
          "end": 297.753,
          "en": "that we're not changing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 298.71,
          "end": 300.06,
          "en": "And therefore, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 300.06,
          "end": 303.33,
          "en": "you should use this function form for updating the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 303.33,
          "end": 306.873,
          "en": "by passing a function to this state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.89,
          "end": 310.59,
          "en": "And this function will automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 310.59,
          "end": 313.11,
          "en": "receive the latest values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.11,
          "end": 316.08299999999997,
          "en": "so the previously stored user input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 317.46,
          "end": 319.47,
          "en": "and should then yield a new object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 319.47,
          "end": 321.42,
          "en": "representing the new state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 321.42,
          "end": 324.303,
          "en": "So here, I'm returning a new state object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 325.26,
          "end": 329.07,
          "en": "where I copy my previous input state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 329.07,
          "end": 331.02,
          "en": "with the spread operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 331.02,
          "end": 333.603,
          "en": "so with these three dots here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 335.1,
          "end": 338.25,
          "en": "and where I then want to override the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 338.25,
          "end": 340.351,
          "en": "for this one input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 340.351,
          "end": 342.551,
          "en": "for which this change handler was triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 343.65,
          "end": 347.28,
          "en": "Now here, we can use a special JavaScript syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 347.28,
          "end": 350.58,
          "en": "where we can set a property dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 350.58,
          "end": 354.54,
          "en": "so where we can dynamically access a property name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 354.54,
          "end": 356.76,
          "en": "by wrapping the identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 356.76,
          "end": 360.72,
          "en": "that contains the property name we want to access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 360.72,
          "end": 362.14,
          "en": "into square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 363.12,
          "end": 366.87,
          "en": "so that we don't set the property named input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 366.87,
          "end": 369.3,
          "en": "but instead we set the property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 369.3,
          "end": 372.033,
          "en": "which name is stored in input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 373.05,
          "end": 378.03,
          "en": "So either current-savings or yearly-contribution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 378.03,
          "end": 381.42,
          "en": "or expected-return or duration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 381.42,
          "end": 384.36,
          "en": "So we're setting one of these four properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 384.36,
          "end": 386.85,
          "en": "depending on what's stored in input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 386.85,
          "end": 388.653,
          "en": "to our value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 389.49,
          "end": 393.57,
          "en": "That's how we can dynamically update this state object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 393.57,
          "end": 396.663,
          "en": "whenever the inputChangeHandler is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 397.53,
          "end": 400.623,
          "en": "And with that, we took an important first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 402.54,
          "end": 404.52,
          "en": "Now at this point, we're not done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 404.52,
          "end": 408.03,
          "en": "regarding managing the user input state though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 408.03,
          "end": 410.1,
          "en": "It's good that we updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 410.1,
          "end": 412.29,
          "en": "whenever an input changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 412.29,
          "end": 415.11,
          "en": "But of course we for example also want to update it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 415.11,
          "end": 417.63,
          "en": "when the resetHandler is triggered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 417.63,
          "end": 420.093,
          "en": "so when the reset button is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 421.53,
          "end": 425.76,
          "en": "Therefore, here, we should also call setUserInput.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 425.76,
          "end": 429.903,
          "en": "And now in the end, reset our state to this initial state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 431.31,
          "end": 433.5,
          "en": "So we can copy this initial state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 433.5,
          "end": 436.83,
          "en": "and also use this here in the resetHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 436.83,
          "end": 441.12,
          "en": "Now copy and pasting is always bad, or not ideal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 441.12,
          "end": 443.71,
          "en": "and therefore I'll instead add a new constant",
